Subject: ptp_get_partial_exif: release the PTP mutex on early error returns

Two early returns left the mutex locked. Note: this PC AutoSave thumbnail
path is still known-broken upstream (the returned offset/length refer to a
temporary buffer, not r->data, and that buffer is leaked). The iOS app does
not call it; PC AutoSave is disabled in the app.

--- a/libfuji/fuji.c
+++ b/libfuji/fuji.c
@@ -589,11 +589,15 @@
 	ptp_mutex_lock(r);
 
 	int rc = fuji_get_events(r);
-	if (rc) return rc;
+	if (rc) {
+		ptp_mutex_unlock(r);
+		return rc;
+	}
 
 	int max_size = 0x4000;
 	rc = ptp_get_partial_object(r, handle, 0, max_size);
 	if (rc == PTP_CHECK_CODE) {
+		ptp_mutex_unlock(r);
 		return PTP_RUNTIME_ERR;
 	}
 	if (rc) {
